  "chapter": 705,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 84 Chapter 705\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4377, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the public health law, in relation to requiring\n        translations of a patient's rights; and in relation to the post-\n        ing of information relating  to  the  long-term  care  ombudsman\n        program\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  legislation  requires  every nursing home in the State to promi-\nnently post, in each resident's room, contact information  for  the  New\nYork  State  Long  Term  Care  Ombudsman Program (LTCOP), the applicable\nregional ombudsman office, and the facility representative. The  nursing\nhome  must  also  update  this contact information for all residents and\ntheir families twice a year. The bill also requires  the  Department  of\nHealth  (DOH)  to  translate  and  make  available  to  the nursing home\npatient's rights pursuant to DOH regulation,  in  the  six  most  common\nnon-English languages based on current census.\n \n  LTCOP was established more than four decades ago as part of the feder-\nal Older Americans Act. Its primary purpose is to advocate for residents\nby  investigating and resolving complaints made by or on behalf of nurs-\ning home residents and promoting the development of resident and  family\ncouncils  as  well  as  working with other government agencies. However,\nresidents need contact information to be able to contact LTCOP  and  the\nDOH to make certain the nursing homes are doing what they need.\n \n  I  support  providing  this information for nursing home residents and\ntheir families. However, in order to better  protect  the  interests  of\nnursing home residents, I have secured an agreement to amend this law in\norder  to require the DOH to translate the nursing home patient's rights\nin the ten most common non-English languages. The Legislature has agreed\nto modification of the posting of contact information for  the  regional\nombudsman and the nursing home complaint hotline to require such posting\nin a conspicuous and customary place, as well as provide the information\ndirectly to the resident and their family/representative.\n \n  On the basis of that agreement, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
